---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Platform — Tracepod"
  description="The Tracepod platform adds a web dashboard, sandbox validation, auto-fix loop, CVE delta reports, fleet policy, and more on top of the open-source toolchain."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="platform-hero section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="eyebrow">Pro platform</div>
      <h1 class="heading-xl platform-headline">
        Container hardening at fleet scale, with the proof that it still runs.
      </h1>
      <p class="body-lg platform-sub">
        The Tracepod platform puts a dashboard, automated validation, and compliance tooling
        on top of the open-source hardening engine. It deploys into your cluster via Helm;
        no data leaves your infrastructure. You see exactly what every workload has been
        hardened to, and whether it passed a live sandbox test.
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Contact us</a>
        <a href="/open-source" class="hero-text-link">or start with open source &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Dashboard screenshot -->
  <section class="screenshot-hero-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="screenshot-slot" role="img" aria-label="Tracepod dashboard overview">
        <img
          src="/screenshots/dashboard.png"
          alt="Tracepod web dashboard showing fleet of hardened workloads, CVE counts, and compliance status"
          loading="lazy"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'; this.nextElementSibling.style.display='flex';"
        />
        <div class="screenshot-placeholder" style="display:none">
          <span>dashboard.png</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Feature sections -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <!-- Feature: Dashboard -->
      <div class="feature-block">
        <div class="feature-block-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Web dashboard</div>
          <h2 class="heading-md">CVE counts, size savings, and coverage for every workload in the cluster.</h2>
          <p class="body-md">
            The dashboard gives you a fleet-wide picture: which workloads have been profiled,
            hardened, validated, and applied. See CVE counts, image size savings, and coverage
            scores at a glance. Drill down to individual builds to inspect the manifest,
            confidence scores, and sandbox results.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li>Fleet summary with attention items (drift, failed validations, missing coverage)</li>
            <li>Per-workload build history and lineage</li>
            <li>Live updates as builds and validations run</li>
            <li>Full audit log, exportable</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-block-visual">
          <div class="screenshot-slot" role="img" aria-label="Tracepod workload detail view">
            <img
              src="/screenshots/workload-detail.png"
              alt="Tracepod workload detail page showing file manifest, confidence scores, and sandbox validation result"
              loading="lazy"
              onerror="this.style.display='none'; this.nextElementSibling.style.display='flex';"
            />
            <div class="screenshot-placeholder" style="display:none"><span>workload-detail.png</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-divider"></div>

      <!-- Feature: Sandbox validation -->
      <div class="feature-block feature-block--reversed">
        <div class="feature-block-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Sandbox validation</div>
          <h2 class="heading-md">Prove the hardened image works before you ship it.</h2>
          <p class="body-md">
            Tracepod spins up an ephemeral copy of your hardened container, cloning the
            workload&rsquo;s pod template (env vars, secrets, config maps, ports). It runs the
            readiness probe, captures logs, and waits for the sensor to report back.
            Missing files are detected and surfaced before the image ever reaches production.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li>Full pod-spec fidelity (env, secrets, ConfigMaps, commands)</li>
            <li>Readiness probe reused as health check</li>
            <li>Missing-file diff against the hardened manifest</li>
            <li>Pass/fail result stored with the build record</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-block-visual sandbox-visual">
          <div class="mini-terminal terminal">
            <div class="terminal-bar">
              <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
              <div class="terminal-dot"></div>
              <span class="terminal-title">sandbox validation</span>
            </div>
            <div class="terminal-body">
              <p><span class="output">Pushing hardened image to sandbox registry&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="output">Creating ephemeral pod in tracepod-sandbox&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="output">Waiting for readiness probe&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="success">&#10003; Pod healthy (12.4s)</span></p>
              <p><span class="output">Capturing sensor profile&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="output">Diffing against hardened manifest&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="success">&#10003; No missing files detected</span></p>
              <p><span class="success">&#10003; Validation PASSED</span></p>
              <p><span class="output">Cleaning up pod&hellip;</span></p>
              <p><span class="success">&#10003; Official image auto-pushed</span></p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-divider"></div>

      <!-- Feature: Auto-fix -->
      <div class="feature-block">
        <div class="feature-block-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Auto-fix loop</div>
          <h2 class="heading-md">Failed validations fix themselves.</h2>
          <p class="body-md">
            When sandbox validation finds missing files, the auto-fix loop rebuilds the image
            with those paths included and validates again, up to three rounds without anyone
            watching. Missing paths come from the sensor diff and from <code>ENOENT</code> lines
            in the container logs. In our postgres test, a build that crashed on missing ICU
            locale data came back green after two rounds.
            Every auto-fixed build keeps its provenance: which build it repaired, and on
            which round. Webhooks fire when the loop finishes, either way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-block-visual">
          <div class="autofix-flow">
            <div class="flow-step flow-step--active">
              <span class="flow-step-num label">01</span>
              <span class="flow-step-label">Validate</span>
              <span class="flow-step-result flow-fail">2 missing files</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">&#8594;</div>
            <div class="flow-step flow-step--active">
              <span class="flow-step-num label">02</span>
              <span class="flow-step-label">Rebuild</span>
              <span class="flow-step-result">+2 paths added</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flow-arrow">&#8594;</div>
            <div class="flow-step flow-step--pass">
              <span class="flow-step-num label">03</span>
              <span class="flow-step-label">Revalidate</span>
              <span class="flow-step-result flow-pass">PASS</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-divider"></div>

      <!-- Feature: CVE delta -->
      <div class="feature-block feature-block--reversed">
        <div class="feature-block-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">CVE delta reports</div>
          <h2 class="heading-md">See exactly how many vulnerabilities you removed.</h2>
          <p class="body-md">
            After each build, Tracepod runs grype against both the source and hardened images
            and computes the delta. CVE counts by severity are stored on the build record and
            surfaced in the dashboard. These are the numbers your security team will ask for.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li>grype scan of source vs hardened image</li>
            <li>Counts broken down by severity</li>
            <li>Stored on the build record, queryable via API</li>
            <li>OpenVEX export with reachability for false-positive suppression</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-block-visual">
          <div class="screenshot-slot" role="img" aria-label="CVE delta report">
            <img
              src="/screenshots/cve-delta.png"
              alt="CVE delta report showing reduction in critical and high severity vulnerabilities after hardening"
              loading="lazy"
              onerror="this.style.display='none'; this.nextElementSibling.style.display='flex';"
            />
            <div class="screenshot-placeholder" style="display:none"><span>cve-delta.png</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-divider"></div>

      <!-- Feature: Fleet policy -->
      <div class="feature-block">
        <div class="feature-block-text">
          <div class="eyebrow">Fleet policy &amp; compliance</div>
          <h2 class="heading-md">Define what &ldquo;hardened&rdquo; means per namespace, then see which workloads miss it.</h2>
          <p class="body-md">
            Define policies per namespace (glob-matched): minimum manifest coverage,
            hardened image required, sandbox validation required.
            The <code>/compliance</code> endpoint evaluates every workload against applicable
            policies and returns a pass/fail matrix you can gate deployments on or feed into
            GRC tooling.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li>Namespace-glob scoped policies</li>
            <li>Min coverage, hardened-required, validated-required</li>
            <li>Fleet compliance report via <code>GET /api/v1/compliance</code></li>
            <li>RBAC-gated: Operator to write, Viewer to read</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-block-visual feature-cards-visual">
          <div class="mini-policy-cards">
            <div class="policy-card">
              <div class="policy-card-ns label">production/*</div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Min coverage</span><span class="policy-val">80%</span></div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Hardened required</span><span class="policy-check">&#10003;</span></div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Validated required</span><span class="policy-check">&#10003;</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="policy-card">
              <div class="policy-card-ns label">staging/*</div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Min coverage</span><span class="policy-val">60%</span></div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Hardened required</span><span class="policy-check">&#10003;</span></div>
              <div class="policy-row"><span>Validated required</span><span class="policy-cross">&mdash;</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-divider"></div>

      <!-- Feature grid: remaining features -->
      <div class="remaining-features">
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="text-align:center; margin-bottom:3rem;">Also in the platform</h2>
        <div class="remaining-grid">

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Apply &amp; drift detection</h3>
            <p>Roll the hardened image out to the live workload from the dashboard (Admin role, with confirmation). The attention panel alerts when the live image drifts from the hardened version.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M18 8h1a4 4 0 0 1 0 8h-1"/>
                <path d="M2 8h16v9a4 4 0 0 1-4 4H6a4 4 0 0 1-4-4V8z"/>
                <line x1="6" y1="1" x2="6" y2="4"/>
                <line x1="10" y1="1" x2="10" y2="4"/>
                <line x1="14" y1="1" x2="14" y2="4"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Webhooks + source-image watching</h3>
            <p>Configure a <code>webhook_url</code> to receive build, validation, and autofix events as JSON. Source-image watching polls upstream digests and triggers auto-rebuild when they change.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/>
                <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/>
                <path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/>
                <path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>RBAC via Kubernetes TokenReview</h3>
            <p>No new identity system. Bearer tokens are validated by the K8s API server. Roles (Viewer, Operator, Admin) are set in a ConfigMap. Works with any OIDC-backed Kubernetes cluster.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/>
                <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/>
                <line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/>
                <line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/>
                <polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Append-only audit log</h3>
            <p>Every action (build, push, validate, apply, policy change) is recorded with user, timestamp, and structured metadata. Exportable as CSV or JSON.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
                <path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>OpenVEX export with reachability</h3>
            <p>Generate machine-readable VEX documents based on whether a vulnerable component is actually present in the minimised image. Suppresses false positives in scanner output.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="remaining-item card">
            <div class="remaining-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true">
                <rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/>
                <line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/>
                <line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Registry management</h3>
            <p>Store target registry configs (host, repository path, tag strategy, TLS, K8s secret) in the platform. Test connectivity before saving. Support for anonymous and authenticated pushes.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-band section">
    <div class="container cta-band-inner">
      <div>
        <h2 class="heading-lg">Book a demo. Bring one workload.</h2>
        <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          We&rsquo;ll show you the hardened image, the CVE delta, and the sandbox pass, live,
          on a workload like yours.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Contact us</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
.platform-hero { padding-top: var(--space-16); }
.hero-text-link {
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  text-decoration: none;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  transition: color var(--transition);
}
.hero-text-link:hover { color: var(--accent); }
.platform-headline { max-width: 800px; margin-top: var(--space-4); }
.platform-sub { max-width: 640px; margin-top: var(--space-6); }
.btn-lg { padding: 0.8rem 1.75rem; font-size: 1rem; }

.screenshot-hero-section { padding-bottom: var(--space-8); }
.screenshot-slot {
  background: var(--bg-elevated);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
  overflow: hidden;
  position: relative;
}
.screenshot-slot img {
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  display: block;
}
.screenshot-placeholder {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
}

.feature-block {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-16);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--space-12) 0;
}
.feature-block--reversed .feature-block-text { order: 2; }
.feature-block--reversed .feature-block-visual { order: 1; }

.feature-block-text {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-4);
}
.feature-block-text code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85em; }

.feature-bullets {
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  padding: 0;
}
.feature-bullets li {
  font-size: 0.9rem;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
  padding-left: 1.2rem;
  position: relative;
}
.feature-bullets li::before {
  content: '\2713';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  color: var(--accent);
  font-size: 0.8rem;
}

.feature-divider {
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--border-subtle);
}

/* Mini terminal */
.mini-terminal { width: 100%; }

/* Autofix flow */
.autofix-flow {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-3);
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-8);
}
.flow-step {
  flex: 1;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  text-align: center;
}
.flow-step-num { font-size: 0.7rem; }
.flow-step-label { font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); }
.flow-step-result { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
.flow-fail { color: #f85149; }
.flow-pass { color: #3fb950; font-weight: 600; }
.flow-arrow { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 1.2rem; flex-shrink: 0; }

/* Policy cards */
.mini-policy-cards {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}
.policy-card {
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--space-4);
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-2);
}
.policy-card-ns { font-size: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
.policy-row {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  color: var(--text-secondary);
}
.policy-val { color: var(--accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; }
.policy-check { color: #3fb950; font-weight: 600; }
.policy-cross { color: var(--text-muted); }

/* Remaining features */
.remaining-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  gap: var(--space-6);
}
.remaining-item {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}
.remaining-icon {
  width: 40px;
  height: 40px;
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--accent-dim);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  color: var(--accent);
}
.remaining-item h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; }
.remaining-item p { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
.remaining-item code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.85em; }

/* CTA band */
.cta-band { background: var(--bg-elevated); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.cta-band-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-8); }

@media (max-width: 960px) {
  .feature-block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-8); }
  .feature-block--reversed .feature-block-text { order: 1; }
  .feature-block--reversed .feature-block-visual { order: 2; }
  .remaining-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  .autofix-flow { flex-direction: column; }
  .flow-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); }
}
@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .remaining-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .cta-band-inner { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
}
</style>
